Package: mfrmr
Type: Package
Title: Estimation and Diagnostics for Many-Facet Measurement Models
Version: 0.2.4.9000
Config/mfrmr/release-status: development
Config/mfrmr/public-version: 0.2.4
Authors@R:
    person(given = "Ryuya", family = "Komuro", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           email = "ryuya.komuro.c4@tohoku.ac.jp",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-9205-0926"))
Description: Estimates many-facet ordered-response
    measurement models with arbitrary facet counts, rating-scale and
    partial-credit parameterizations, a generalized partial-credit extension
    with discrimination varying across levels of one selected facet.
    Marginal maximum likelihood permits a different facet to own category
    steps; joint maximum likelihood requires the same facet for both roles.
    Conditional maximum likelihood fits many-facet rating-scale and
    partial-credit models by conditioning on person totals, with structural
    contrast intervals and no assumed ability distribution.
    Experimental two-family estimation and conditional scoring retain explicit
    uncertainty limitations. The fit, diagnose and report workflow covers
    anchoring, linking, bias and differential-functioning screening, with saved
    results for replay. Observed-score G-Study and D-Study analyses
    support assessment planning under declared rating designs. Agreement,
    rater feedback and conditional classification summaries connect analysis
    to assessment decisions. See 'Andrich'
    (1978) <doi:10.1007/BF02293814>, 'Masters' (1982)
    <doi:10.1007/BF02296272>, and 'Muraki' (1992)
    <doi:10.1177/014662169201600206> for the underlying ordered-response
    models.
